<main>
  <p class="eyebrow">henk</p>
  <h1>Your app answered — with an error.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    This one isn't henk. DNS, routing, the certificate and the dev server are all working:
    henk forwarded the request, and your app handed back a server error. The fix is in your
    app, not in the proxy.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to look</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>The terminal running your dev server.</strong>
      <p>
        The stack trace is there — henk only relays the status code, it never sees the
        exception.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your app's own logs.</strong>
      <p>
        <code>storage/logs/laravel.log</code>, <code>docker compose logs -f</code>, or
        whatever your framework writes to.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="fix">
    Nothing to change in henk — <strong><code>henk doctor</code></strong> will confirm the
    routing is healthy if you want to rule it out.
  </p>
</main>
